BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering — Sebastopol Center For the A
 rts\, California
DTSTART:20260501T000000
DTEND:20260502T000000
UID:e92065ef1ec7da1c4870cde7bb39ca96@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering for Remembrance and Peace\,
  May\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $10.00\n        \n      \n  
   \n  \n\nFriday\, May 1\, 2026\; 1:30 – 4:00pmDue to limited capacity\,
  we are asking for a suggested donation of $10 to confirm your attendance.
  Bring a copy of your receipt at check-in to Painting/Drawing Studio adjac
 ent to Ceramics StudioJoin us for a monthly\, heart-centered gathering whe
 re we come together to create Jizo guardians out of clay—symbols of comp
 assion\, protection\, and peace. Rooted in the Buddhist tradition and echo
 ed across many cultures\, Jizo figures traditionally honor children and al
 l who have passed\, those in transition\, and those in distress.This ongoi
 ng project is dedicated to remembering those lost to war\, with a special 
 focus now on the approximately 19\,000 children who have perished in Israe
 l and Gaza in recent years. Through the simple\, meditative act of working
  with clay\, we create benevolent beings that will become part of public e
 xhibits and peace sites\, offering spaces for reflection\, mourning\, and 
 hope. Our gatherings conclude with a gentle ritual to honor the lives of t
 hese children.Located in the Painting & Drawing Room. The gathering is ope
 n to ages 12 - adult\, and no prior clay experience is necessary—all cla
 y and basic materials are supplied. Registration is required to participat
 e.Donations are welcome to help cover materials and expenses. More than a 
 class\, this is a shared space of warmth and care—an opportunity to tend
  to our own hearts while taking part in love in action.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n 
              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/jizo-peace-project-clay-gathe
 ring-may
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pt. 3: Finding One’s Voice Through Art – A Second Life in Cera
 mics with Ping Zhong — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260502T000000
DTEND:20260503T000000
UID:81832a52f7f272fc5bd0f2c33221974a@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Pt. 3: Finding One’s Voice Through Art – A Second Life in 
 Ceramics with Ping Zhong\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $10.00\n
         \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, May 2\, 2026\; 2-3pmLocated in th
 e Fireside RoomSebArts’ Ceramics Residency Artist\, Ping Zhong\, will sh
 are their personal journey of discovering artistic expression through cera
 mics later in life\, introducing their work and experiences to illustrate 
 how art can become a meaningful path of self-discovery.Due to limited capa
 city of the Ceramics Studio\, we are asking for a suggested donation of $1
 0 to confirm your attendance. About the Artist: Ping Zhong’s artistic pr
 actice is a continuous exploration of regeneration—of materials\, forms\
 , and cultural narratives. She investigates the dialogue between ancient C
 hinese pottery and contemporary visual language\, using wheel-throwing\, h
 and-building\, and sculpture to create works in which history and personal
  growth converge. This reinterpretation of classical forms is not only an 
 artistic method\, but also a philosophical inquiry into the harmony betwee
 n past and future. Deeply motivated to uncover the potential within clay\,
  Ping pushes the boundaries of design and technique. Her work reflects on 
 universal themes: the individual’s place within the community\, the rela
 tionship between essence and appearance\, and the evolving connection betw
 een nature and society. Through these explorations\, she seeks to create a
 rt that resonates across cultures.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n      
           Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/pt-3-finding-ones-voice-throu
 gh-art-a-second-life-in-ceramics-with-ping-zhong
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Explore Gel Plate Printing — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Ca
 lifornia
DTSTART:20260502T000000
DTEND:20260503T000000
UID:640f56ac648ef534e104d99f8e73bd99@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Explore Gel Plate Printing\, 5/2\n\n  \n    \n      \n        
 \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, May 2\, 2026
 \; 11 AM – 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials feeAge: 16+ Participants: min. 
 8Learn to create beautiful designs on paper by printing with a gel plate a
 nd acrylic paint. Mixed media artist Catherine Cruz will teach you the bas
 ic skills for using this fun tool from printing textural backgrounds\, to 
 layering colors\, and using stencils and other applications. You will take
  home many prints that can be used for designing collage\, mixed media art
  or greeting cards. This class is suitable for anyone wanting to learn thi
 s unique mono printing style and perfect for beginners.What you’ll get f
 rom this workshop: Methods for applying paint and pulling successful print
 s (Note: Magazine image transfer is not included in this class.)\, Techniq
 ues for creating intricate layered designs\, Creative use of mark-making t
 ools and masks\, Strategies for combining techniques.A variety of papers w
 ill be provided but you are highly encouraged to bring your own papers to 
 experiment on.IMPORTANT: Instructions for where to purchase your materials
  and how to prepare them is provided in the attached PDF. The instructor w
 ill start the class with a demonstration so please arrive a few minutes ea
 rly to get set up so we can start on time.  We will take a short break for
  lunch between 12:30 and 1:00 pm so bring your lunch and a beverage.  Abou
 t the instructor: Catherine Cruz is a French-American artist whose work is
  informed by textures and patterns created by the passing of time and the 
 effects of the natural elements on the built environment.  She holds a Bac
 helor of Science in interior design and she worked in the field of archite
 ctural design and green building certification for over 25 years.  She has
  taught collage and mixed media workshops in the Bay Area and in France si
 nce 2019\, and this is her fifth year at the Sebastopol Center for the Art
 s.  Her studio is located in Sebastopol and she participates in Art Trails
  Open Studios.  You may contact Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Ch
 eck out Catherine’s other classes here:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual
 -arts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n          \n            \n              \n                Add to car
 t
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/explore-gel-plate-printing-52
