SUMMARY:Ultra Textural Weaving on a Unique Substrate — Sebastopol Center
  For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260523T000000
DTEND:20260524T000000
UID:739909d2e70ea79fb973352bd0407f4a@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Ultra Textural Weaving on a Unique Substrate\n\n  \n    \n    
   \n        \n          $150.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, 
 May 23\, 2026\; 10AM - 3PM$125 + $25 Materials FeeYou’ll learn many tech
 niques for weaving\, knotting\, wrapping\, tying\, sewing\, coiling and tw
 isting of fiber materials to build our dynamic and stunning pieces to hang
  on the wall. The surprising and versatile foundation for the weaving is p
 lastic fencing\, which opens the creative journey into much more than ordi
 nary weaving. You'll have access to plastic fencing\, many gorgeous fabric
 s and yarns\, beads\, buttons and other decorations to add to your piece. 
 You’ll also make fringe\, tassels and pompoms to add texture and delight
 . No art or weaving experience is necessary\, and all levels are most welc
 ome. (If you've taken Vicki's other weaving workshop\, please note that th
 is will be a very different workshop\, with plenty of new techniques to le
 arn and outcomes to explore).Please bring: Sewing needle and thread\, Fabr
 ic Scissors (If you have them)Optional: Feel free to bring materials from 
 your own stash including fabrics\, yarn\, string\, lace\, ribbon\, beads\,
  old jewelry parts and other decorations.About the Instructor: Vicki Asseg
 ued is an experimental and innovative fiber artist and instructor\, always
  finding new and unique ways to work with textiles and fibers. Through her
  creative process\, she explores many ways to weave\, layer\, attach\, coi
 l\, tie\, knot\, twist\, build and develop her pieces so they are vibrant 
 and engaging. She then shares all of her techniques with her students\, su
 pporting and inspiring them to fully engage in their own creative process 
 of discovery and expression. Vicki teaches at art schools and retreats aro
 und the country\, such as the Art & Soul Mixed Media Retreat\, the Mendoci
 no Art Center\, North Country Studio Workshops and the San Jose Museum of 
 Quilts & Textiles. Vicki completed a 4-month residency with the Santa Cruz
  Recycled Art Program. She has exhibited and sold her work at galleries\, 
 businesses\, health centers\, restaurants\, community centers\, museums\, 
 and open studio events. You can learn more about Vicki here: https://www.v
 ickiart.com/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
