  \n          $170.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, June 27\, 2
 026 10AM - 4PMCost: $130 + $40 materials feeEase into summer with a day of
  watercolor inspired by Sonoma County’s sun-soaked abundance—ripe berr
 ies\, figs\, citrus\, fragrant herbs\, wild grasses\, and golden light str
 etching into the evening. Juicy reds\, warm yellows\, and deep greens set 
 the mood for loose\, luminous paintings that feel relaxed\, ripe\, and del
 iciously seasonal.Focus on building strong compositions using color\, text
 ure\, light\, and form\, developed through wet washes\, controlled washes\
 , and textural techniques. Guided discussions explore the essential elemen
 ts of visual art to help you create expressive\, individual work.All mater
 ials provided\, Space limited to 10 studentsDiscussion break 12:30pm. Plea
 se bring a brown bag lunchAbout the Instructor: Lynn Zachreson studied art
  at the University of Minnesota and San Jose State University—Painting\,
  Printmaking: BA Fine Art. She has experience teaching all ages: Watercolo
 r painting skills\, 30+ years\, Watercolor figure painting 20+ years\, and
  Fine Art Basics with Mixed Media 20+ years. Lynn enjoys spending her time
  painting\, teaching\, long distance hiking\, and gardening. View Lynn’s
  art here: https://lynnzachresonart.com/\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n          
